# The loop counts up to the length of the string, and a turn calls nothing: it ends within its data. No copy of the loop polls, and nothing in the function does.
# CHECK-LABEL: name="countSpaces" role=Source
# CHECK-NOT: isLoopPoll
# CHECK-NOT: :LoopHint)
# CHECK-LABEL: end of function
# The loop is there: eight characters a turn, then one a turn for the rest, and the copy for strings of 16-bit characters.
# LOOPS-LABEL: steps by 8
